      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes requested** — See inline comments for details. [[trajectory](go/traj/f0360b44-0ed8-4f8f-89e8-bb4aea35f524)]\n\n### Review Summary\n\n**Functionality**\nThe change correctly addresses the false validation failures on the final image chunk. By performing the frame buffer validation against `current_frame_size` before applying `FP_SENSOR_IMAGE_OFFSET`, it ensures that the host-requested chunk bounds are correctly evaluated.\n\n**Security**\n❌ **Critical Issue:** A potential Out-Of-Bounds (OOB) read vulnerability is introduced. Because `FP_SENSOR_IMAGE_OFFSET` is added to `offset` *after* `validate_fp_buffer_offset` completes, the new `offset` can cause the final read bounds (`offset + size`) to exceed the physical `sizeof(fp_buffer)` if `current_frame_size + FP_SENSOR_IMAGE_OFFSET \u003e sizeof(fp_buffer)`. An explicit bounds check against `sizeof(fp_buffer)` must be added before the `memcpy` operation. See the inline comment for a suggested fix.\n\n**Style \u0026 Consistency**\nThe code style is consistent with the surrounding codebase. The comment explaining the offset addition was appropriately moved alongside the logic.\n\n**Testing**\nThe CL description notes that manual testing using `ectool` was performed for different modes (vendor format and pattern), which is appropriate.",
